Unreleased
==========

Symbolic trie
-------------

- Added an in-memory symbolic-trie index with configurable 2-, 4-, or 8-way
  fanout, leaf capacity, sampled root splitting, and entropy × variance-based
  splits.
- Stores MBRs and selects split dimensions across the full transform word
  (up to 64 dimensions); record lower bounds use the leading 16 dimensions.
- Supports SAX, SFA, PISA, and SPARTAN words, including integer input files,
  optional z-normalization, and query-specific symbolic lower-bound tables.
- Uses node-MBR pruning plus best-first leaf scans, ordered by record lower
  bounds, with exact-distance early abandonment.
- Provides batch and single-query parallel modes with configurable worker and
  queue counts, plus construction, coverage, and per-phase query timings.
- Reports split occupancy, non-empty-child, and largest-child diagnostics to
  make fanout experiments directly comparable.

iSAX
----

- Added dynamic, variance-driven root-cardinality splitting for symbolic
  transforms and support for SAX, SFA, PISA, and SPARTAN words.
- Added full-word node MBR pruning and transform-specific lower bounds,
  including SIMD-capable exact-distance paths where available.
- Improved parallel index construction and hybrid query scheduling, including
  configurable worker/queue counts and robust queue ownership.
- Unified iSAX and trie benchmark summaries, CSV logs, coverage reporting,
  construction timings, and optional per-phase query profiling.

Benchmark runners
-----------------

- `run_dataset.sh` now prints compact K/M/G configuration counts and an
  end-of-run table of query work, coverage, and wall time for all methods run.
- `run_suite.sh` accepts `--index-type isax|trie` to run a regular suite across
  all configured datasets with either layout.
- iSAX runner methods use variance-driven root cardinalities by default;
  trie MBR/split dimensions follow each dataset's coefficient setting and can
  be overridden with `--trie-mbr-dims`; trie fanout is configurable with
  `--trie-fanout 2|4|8`.
